
# Local environment.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in to work on accounts locally:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Leave it empty — or skip the file entirely — and the site runs exactly as it
# does in production without Supabase: every guide, learning topic and practice
# question works, signed out, with study progress kept in the browser. Only
# sign-in and cross-device sync are switched off.

# Supabase project settings -> API.
#   SUPABASE_URL      the "Project URL"
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY the "anon public" key
#
# The anon key is meant to be public and is constrained by the row level
# security policies in supabase/schema.sql. The service_role key is NOT used
# anywhere in this app and must never be put here — it bypasses those policies.
#
# Note these are not NEXT_PUBLIC_*. Nothing in this app talks to Supabase from
# the browser, so they stay server-side and are read at runtime rather than
# being baked into the bundle at build time.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
